00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.810
The robbers washed themselves of the smell of winter,

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:39.930
and after their transformation,

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:46.600
spring descended like a shout of joy upon the woods around Mattis' fort.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.660
The snow melted,

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:51.240
and the river roared, foamed,

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.850
and sang with all its waterfalls.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.840
Hey!

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.460
At last their splendid robbers' life was beginning again!

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:08.220
In the Great Spring

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:08.220
In the Great Spring

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:50.220
Standing here, I can feel the winter melting out of me.

00:02:54.780 --> 00:03:00.140
Soon, I'll be so light I can fly!

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.350
Then give it a try.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:32.460
There's sure to be some wild harpies flying around. You can join their flock.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.590
Yeah, I'll give it a shot!

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.360
Come on!

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.000
I'd like to catch a wild horse!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.930
A bear or wolf must have scared them.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.900
Otherwise why would they be so frightened?

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.920
No,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.420
they're not frightened.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:46.050
They're just running the winter out of their bodies.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.960
When they're tired of that and begin to graze,

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:56.690
I'm going to catch one and take it home to Mattis' fort.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.450
I've wanted to do that for a long time.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.090
Why would you want to bring it to the fort?

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.480
Riding is for the woods, right?

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:09.570
We might as well catch two, and ride them right away.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:16.080
Oh, I see even the Borka clan <i>can</i> have brains in their heads.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.120
Okay, we'll do that!

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.900
Let's give it a go!

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.540
It seems like they won't be here for a while yet.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:02.180
I'm enjoying just sitting here, soaking up the spring.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:12.700
I like you for that,

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.140
Birk Borkason.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.620
You're right, Birk.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:35.580
Why should I take a horse away from the woods, where he belongs?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.080
But I do want to ride.

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.730
And now it's time!

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.310
How about those two?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.310
Uh-huh.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.410
That's our first loot this year.

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:40.840
Let's go!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.310
Roger!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.000
Quick, tie it up!

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.120
Yeah!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.560
Got it!

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.820
We have to ride them!

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.070
But...

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.030
These two aren't going to just let us ride them on our first try.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:53.140
Yeah. First, they need to understand that we mean them no harm.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.810
I've got an idea!

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:06.920
Here.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.140
Eat up!

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:39.720
If I hadn't pulled my hand back as fast as I did, 
he'd have bitten off my fingers

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.130
and I'd be walking home to Mattis with them dangling from my belt.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:48.250
Good grief, he's such a rascal.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.140
"Rascal". That's a good name.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.150
I'll call him that.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.660
Then you'll have to give mine a name in exchange.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.160
Let's see...

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:14.160
They're both equally crazy.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.480
You can call him "Reckless".

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:19.410
Yup.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.640
Hey! Listen up, wild horses.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:28.960
We've given you names.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.680
They're "Rascal" and "Reckless",

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:39.610
and you belong to us now, whether you like it or not.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.060
Understand?

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:43.480
Rascal. Reckless.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:51.700
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:51.700
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.860
Wheats, furs, and great treasures!

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:12.880
Such a prosperous start!

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:27.700
Mattis!

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:31.370
Hand those treasures over to us.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:37.360
It seems you're a little late.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:41.610
I'm not giving you anything, not even a single coin!

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.420
Let's go!

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:46.170
C-Crap!

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.280
Damn it!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.480
Now just listen, Mattis!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:05.820
We managed to weather the harsh winter somehow, but everyone's exhausted.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:10.250
Do you think I'll give you all my treasure just because of your sob story?

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:13.530
I'm not asking for all of it.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.740
Half would be just fine!

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:17.330
Shut up!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.750
Get lost already!

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:21.250
Hey! Hey!

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:22.810
Stop it!

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.730
Hey, piss off!

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:29.500
Damn, you are such a jerk...

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:35.010
If I just walk away empty-handed, 
I'll be too ashamed to look Undis in the face.

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.690
Serves you right!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:45.610
The boss of Borka's robbers goes out hunting just because he's scared of his wife?!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.480
Wait until all my robber friends hear this!

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.090
You're no different!

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:56.330
Don't flatter yourself just because I acted humbly!

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:11.140
Hold up! Wait!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.130
Guys, don't be so hasty!

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:40.940
They must be thirsty.

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.370
We must take them to water.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:44.970
Let's take them to the marsh.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:48.220
There they can't drink it all up too easily.

00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:49.180
Yup.

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:43.600
We've tamed them at last.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.450
Yes, we have.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:17:00.570
When I said I wanted to ride, I meant it.

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:01.790
Understand?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.290
Now then, Rowd—

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:07.720
I won't be riding any more today.

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.130
Me neither.

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:56.140
You whiled away the whole day enjoying the spring...

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.300
Now I need to think up a way to explain to Mattis

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:07.930
why I needed to stay out soaking up the spring for so long.

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.050
Sturkus!

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:04.010
What happened to you?!

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:08.020
Borka's robbers!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:10.510
Those dirty devils!

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:13.780
Those scoundrels!

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.920
Just you wait!

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.200
Next time I see them,

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:26.750
I'll grab each one of his robbers and knock them down into the pits of hell!

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:27.930
Mattis.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:43.710
People like Borka should be hanged.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.720
What happened?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:52.720
Mattis and his brave boys had been lying in wait on Robbers' Walk,

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:58.100
when by good fortune, a whole mass of travelers passed by.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.810
Merchants with provisions and skins, and a pile of money too.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.480
They had no way of defending themselves.

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:13.000
You can guess what happened.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:18.110
When we had just loaded everything on our horses' backs and were heading homeward...

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:29.600
I see...

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.700
That's when Sturkus took an arrow.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.270
We fired back right away.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:41.770
Oh yes, there must have been a couple of them who fared as badly as Sturkus!

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:49.580
Just wait.

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:51.780
This is only the beginning.

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:57.270
I'll crush each one of them in turn!

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:00.670
Up till now I've held my peace...

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:06.800
But now I'll put an end to all of Borka's robbers!

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:15.350
And what if that's the end of all of Mattis' robbers too?

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:18.080
You haven't thought of that, have you?!

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:23.640
I don't intend to think about that!

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:28.320
Why? Because it's not going to happen!

00:22:30.490 --> 00:22:33.040
You can't know that.

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:48.280
They couldn't finish me off the first time around.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:50.930
No, Sturkus.

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:56.200
They couldn't finish you off the first time around.

00:22:59.300 --> 00:23:02.030
Outwardly she shed no tears,

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:07.860
but in her heart, she was weeping grievously.

